docs {
  # GET /author-information/{id}
  
  Retrieves public instructor profile fields and published course IDs.
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `GET`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/author-information/:id`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **Public** when the user's public profile layout is not private (`permission_public_author`).
  - Bearer JWT optional.
  
  ## Public vs private fields
  
  Always returned:
  - `ID`, `display_name`, `user_nicename`, `courses` (published instructor course IDs)
  
  Added only when `RestAuth::can_view_user_private_fields( target_user_id )` is true (self, users with `list_users`, or instructor of a course the target is enrolled in):
  - `user_login`, `user_email`, `user_registered`, `user_url`
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `id` | `integer` | **Yes** | Instructor user ID. |
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK — public fields
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_author",
    "message": "Author details retrieved successfully",
    "data": {
      "ID": 1,
      "display_name": "Jane Doe",
      "user_nicename": "jane_instructor",
      "courses": [105, 110, 120]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ### 200 OK — with private fields
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_author",
    "message": "Author details retrieved successfully",
    "data": {
      "ID": 1,
      "display_name": "Jane Doe",
      "user_nicename": "jane_instructor",
      "courses": [105, 110, 120],
      "user_login": "jane",
      "user_email": "jane@example.com",
      "user_registered": "2024-01-01 00:00:00",
      "user_url": "https://example.com"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ### 404 Not Found
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_author",
    "message": "Author not found",
    "data": {
      "status": 404
    }
  }
  ```
}
